{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Close prep done; ONE step remains (attestation deliberately staled)\n\nState as of handoff:\n\n- Change **2704 patch set 3 is MERGED** (`b3609ce73816`, \"Trust a lagging checkout's silence less\").\n- All **6 acceptance criteria are ticked**, on the evidence in the agent's report above: the\n  mechanism proven at runtime (AC1), the allow-after-refresh path (AC2), defect-seeded tests RED\n  against unmodified `src/` (AC3), the still-refuse direction for a genuinely commit-less target in\n  a complete checkout (AC4), the close gate's HEAD-scoped scan pinned unchanged (AC5), and the MCP\n  `link_tickets` path proven **through the tool** rather than inferred from the library (AC6).\n- **`file_impact` widened from 3 paths to 4**: the merged commit also changed\n  `docs/ticket-model.md`, which the reviewed plan did not declare. The close gate refuses on that\n  gap (\"the work went beyond the reviewed plan\"), correctly — a reviewer who approved a 3-file plan\n  did not approve a 4-file change.\n\n**Next step, for whoever resumes:** widening `file_impact` is a material plan change, so it staled\nthe signed plan-review attestation by design. The close will refuse with `stale-material` until a\nfresh review runs. The sequence is:\n\n```\nrebar review-plan 009f-5f7f-07a5-4b36          # expect PASS; ~15-20 min, do NOT wrap in a timeout\nrebar transition 009f-5f7f-07a5-4b36 in_progress closed --class <class>\n```\n\nRun the close from a worktree that provably reaches `b3609ce73816`\n(`git merge-base --is-ancestor b3609ce73816 HEAD`). Close class is a judgement call I am leaving\nopen: this is arguably `preexisting` (the HEAD-only scan was always wrong for a replica checkout and\nnothing regressed), but whoever closes should decide on the ticket's own history rather than inherit\nmy guess.\n\n**Do not `--force` past either gate.** If the close reports `GATE_CONGESTED`, that is host\ncongestion and not a verdict — the 4-slot semaphore is shared across checkouts and was frequently\nsaturated by other sessions tonight. Wait for a slot and retry; the attestation stays valid."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788669640911941001,"uuid":"e46a3859-d8a0-4eb8-a535-db234e1bd628"}